# Scope

| File | Change |
| --- | --- |
| [`ciel_runtime_support/provider_responses_passthrough.py`](../../../../../../../ciel_runtime_support/provider_responses_passthrough.py) | Import `gateway_route_selected` from `initial_stream_retry`. In `_forward_buffered_stream`: `retries = 0 if gateway_route_selected(config) else self._stream_truncation_retries(config)`. Nothing else. |
| [`tests/test_provider_responses_gateway_replay_guard.py`](../../../../../../../tests/test_provider_responses_gateway_replay_guard.py) | New dedicated file, 4 tests (8 selected-gateway subcases, 2 control subcases). |

Task-only diff: [`native-retry-boundary-evidence/production.diff`](native-retry-boundary-evidence/production.diff). It was produced against a reconstruction of the pre-edit file whose SHA-256 is `11454fbd...20df`, identical to the file left by the passthrough-read-failure task, so the diff contains this change only.

Not edited: `tests/test_meta_provider.py`, `initial_stream_retry.py`, the overlay, the transport, routers, or any other concurrently edited file. No config, remote, live, commit, push or deploy action.

This closes the gap listed in `retry-boundaries.okf` ("It does not change the native Responses path ... that path is `provider_responses_passthrough.py`, owned by another agent").

# Design

- Guard key is the same helper the other two replay sites use: `gateway_route_selected(config)` = `isinstance(config, Mapping) and bool(config.get(ROUTE_TOKEN_KEY))`. No provider-name branch.
- Why a replay reaches the same gateway: `_forward_buffered_stream` opens the same `request` object (same URL) with the same `pcfg=config` on every attempt. The new test asserts the open carries the overlay token and a gateway URL.
- Buffering decision unchanged: `forward` still uses `completion_gate or self._stream_truncation_retries(config)`. A selected-gateway config with a configured count stays buffered, so a truncated stream raises `UpstreamStreamReadError(attempts=1, downstream_started=False)` with no status line and no bytes sent. That is the same exit an exhausted budget already uses.
- No retries added. The only behavior change is that an existing replay window closes for a token-carrying config. Unchanged: the log text (`attempt={attempt}/{retries}` now never prints for routed configs), terminal detection, the read-error-after-terminal handling, and the completion continuation.

