Runner: [`run_focused.py`](native-retry-boundary-evidence/run_focused.py), a copy of the retry-boundaries runner. It removes every inherited `CIEL_RUNTIME_*`, sets a temp `CIEL_RUNTIME_CONFIG_DIR`, a free `CIEL_RUNTIME_ROUTER_PORT` and `CIEL_RUNTIME_TEST_ISOLATED=1`. The test class also clears `CIEL_RUNTIME_*` in `setUp`.

- Fail before ([`before.txt`](native-retry-boundary-evidence/before.txt)), passthrough `11454fbd...20df`: 4 tests, 6 failures. All 6 selected-gateway subcases (`eof_after_created`, `incomplete_read_partial`, `tls_eof_after_created`, each with and without the completion gate) failed `AssertionError: 1 != 3`: three upstream dispatches to the same gateway. The 3 control tests passed.
- Pass after ([`after.txt`](native-retry-boundary-evidence/after.txt)), passthrough `3a0e8339...36ff`: 4 tests OK.
- HEAD `572b7e7` export plus only the prior task helper `initial_stream_retry.py`, `production.diff` and the new test ([`head-plus-change.txt`](native-retry-boundary-evidence/head-plus-change.txt)): 4 tests OK. The change does not depend on the passthrough read-failure edit by the other agent.
- Focused and architecture suites ([`focused-suites.txt`](native-retry-boundary-evidence/focused-suites.txt)): 22 files, 636 tests OK, 42 skipped. Includes architecture_contracts, architecture_budget, meta_provider (run only), provider_responses_completion_gate, openai_responses_upstream_stream_error, remote_bridge_http, alibaba/xai providers, initial_stream_retry, runaway_collection_retry, gateway overlay/transport/central_fallback/gateways, provider_network, upstream_retry, upstream_error_policy. These ran against the working tree including other agents uncommitted edits at that time.
- Imports and lint ([`imports-and-ruff.txt`](native-retry-boundary-evidence/imports-and-ruff.txt)): fresh `python -I` import of passthrough, initial_stream_retry and overlay without `CIEL_RUNTIME_*` (no import cycle). `ruff check` on both files and `ruff check .`: All checks passed (local ruff 0.14.11).
- Live router 127.0.0.1:9512 `/health` ok, pid 31392, before and after all runs.

# Test cases

- Selected gateway (real `CielAiRouterGatewayOverlay.apply` config, `responses_stream_truncation_retries: 2`), truncated raw stream: one dispatch, `attempts == 1`, `downstream_started` false, no body, no `send_response`, no `provider_responses_stream_retry` log, `provider_responses_stream_truncated ... attempts=1` logged.
- Unoverlaid control (central config, and `discovery_provider_config` of the overlay copy, token removed), retries 2: 3 dispatches, `attempts == 3`, 2 retry logs, no body.
- Unoverlaid config, attempt 1 `IncompleteRead(partial)` without terminal, attempt 2 full terminal stream: 2 dispatches, the complete stream is delivered once with status 200 (existing recovery behavior).
- Selected gateway, complete stream with terminal (with and without completion gate): one dispatch, bytes delivered unchanged, status 200 once.

# Reachability (limits the claim)

- In shipped code only `providers/alibaba.py:723` sets `responses_stream_truncation_retries` (=1). The overlay mints the token only for `cielairouter`. So in default configuration a CielAiRouter config already has 0 truncation replays, and this guard changes behavior only when a CielAiRouter provider config carries a user-set nonzero `responses_stream_truncation_retries`. Verified by grep of `ciel_runtime_support` and `ciel_runtime.py`.
- Not verified in this task: an end-to-end Codex request through a running router that reaches `_forward_buffered_stream` with the overlay copy. No live or remote request was made.
- Pre-existing and unchanged (see passthrough-read-failure-fix.okf item 1): a read error after a parsed terminal event on the buffered path still fails the attempt; for a routed config that now fails without a replay.
